      "name": "semantic_search",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 19, \"items_by_type\": {\"column_concept\": [{\"id\": \"column_concept_master_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Master subject identifier columns (MASTER_SUBJECT_ID and its sortable variant MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT) replicated across the registrar offering tables, the subject summary, the textbook program, the library reserve program, and the CIS course catalog. For clustered subjects (e.g. joint or cross-listed offerings), the master subject identifier points to the leading subject of the cluster, so joining on it matches offerings that share the same master subject even when their own SUBJECT_ID differs. SUBJECT_ID/SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the subject itself, while MASTER_SUBJECT_ID/MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the cluster's master; the _SORT columns are the sortable forms of the same values used for cross-table joins.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_term_code\", \"desc\": \"Term code columns in YYYYTT format (e.g. '2025FA', '2019SP', '2021JA', '2012SU'; TT = FA Fall, SP Spring, JA January/IAP, SU Summer) appearing across term dimension and fact tables. They are the universal join key linking subject offerings, textbook materials, library reserves, and IAP activities to term attributes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Subject identifier columns shared across catalog, registrar, textbook-program, and library tables. SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (e.g. '18.01'); it appears in every subject-related fact table but at different grains and program scopes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_total_units\", \"desc\": \"Total credit unit columns replicated across catalog and registrar subject tables. They represent the same business quantity (total credit units of a subject) but come from different processes and pair with different companion unit columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_year_columns\", \"desc\": \"Year columns across term, catalog, and time dimension tables representing different year systems: academic year, fiscal year, financial aid year, and degree year. Selecting the correct year system is essential for yearly grouping and partitioning.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_material_status_key\", \"desc\": \"Material status key columns of the textbook program (TIP) and library reserve program. Both are coded status references decoded by their own lookup tables (key value equals code value), with independent value domains: TIP statuses ('RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options, 'RC' Recommended, 'PC' Val-u option, 'BR' Bookstore recommends, 'CL' Go to class first, 'NM' Course has no materials, 'U' Unknown, plus NULL-description keys) vs library reserve statuses ('U' Unknown, 'R' null description, 'N' Non-Required Course Material, 'O' Reserve only, 'X' No Required Textbook, 'Y' Required Course Material).\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_hass_attribute\", \"desc\": \"HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute code and description columns. The code columns appear in the three course catalog feeds and in the CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE lookup; description columns exist in three variants: the catalog-embedded HASS_ATTRIBUTE_DESC, the lookup's DESCRIPTION_ON_FORM (registration-form wording), and DESCRIPTION_IN_BULLETIN (short bulletin wording). Selecting the right description variant depends on the wording requested by the question.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_type_site\", \"desc\": \"Building classification columns replicated across the current and historical building tables of both table families: BUILDING_TYPE ('ACADEMIC', 'SERVICE', 'RESIDENT') and SITE ('MIT', 'BATES', 'LINC', 'BOS', etc.). They carry the same value domain but differ in time semantics: the building-table columns are the current classification, while the history-table columns are the classification recorded at each fiscal period, so filtering by one versus the other can select different building sets.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_dlc_key\", \"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key columns (values like 'D_AEROASTRO', 'D_IDSS', 'D_BIOLOGY') identifying a DLC across the facilities, HR, space, and academic-department domains. They are the universal cross-domain join key linking facilities organizations and space units to HR organization units, the master department hierarchy, and academic departments. Naming and completeness vary: DLC_KEY in most tables, D_CODE in MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, DLC_CODE in the master hierarchy tables; some columns carry composite values ('D_DSL:HQ') or nulls.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_office_location\", \"desc\": \"OFFICE_LOCATION columns recording where a person's office/desk is, replicated across the person-directory tables (SE_PERSON, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY, DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY). All hold a building or building-room text identifier in the same value domain as FCLT_ROOMS.BUILDING_ROOM, but they describe different populations (employee/person master vs student vs primary employee directory vs Drupal employee feed) and differ sharply in non-null coverage and in how many values are building-room ('BLDG-ROOM') versus building-only ('BLDG'). Choosing the right column determines whose office is reported and whether room-level joins to FCLT_ROOMS succeed.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_fiscal_period\", \"desc\": \"Fiscal period code columns in YYYYMM format (e.g. '199602' = FY1996 period 2, '201505') appearing in two distinct roles: as the primary key of the month-grain time dimension (TIME_MONTH.FISCAL_PERIOD, also mirrored in TIME_DAY.FISCAL_PERIOD for day-to-month linkage), and as the snapshot-period stamp of the facilities historical tables (FCLT_BUILDING_HIST, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1, FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_HIST, FCLT_FLOOR_HIST, FCLT_ROOMS_HIST, FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST). Both roles share the same YYYYMM value domain, but the time dimension uses it for calendar grouping while the history tables use it to mark when a facilities snapshot was taken.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_access_level\", \"desc\": \"Access level columns recorded at three granularity levels of the facilities domain plus the space-planning room feed: building-level ACCESS_LEVEL_CODE/ACCESS_LEVEL_NAME (current and per-fiscal-period history), floor-level ACCESS_LEVEL, and room-level ACCESS_LEVEL (FCLT_ROOMS, FAC_ROOMS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD). They share a numeric value domain (observed 0-3) but describe the access restriction of different physical objects or come from different feeds, so filters and joins must target the granularity and table family the question refers to.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_num_of_rooms\", \"desc\": \"NUM_OF_ROOMS columns recording how many rooms a building contains, replicated across the current and historical building tables of both families. The building-table columns hold the current room count (one value per building); the history-table columns hold the room count at each fiscal period, used for room-count statistics (average, range, variance, minimum) across a building's history records.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_room\", \"desc\": \"Combined building-room identifier columns (e.g. '1-080') appearing in both the space assignment fact table and the facilities room inventory. They identify the same physical room concept but come from different business processes with different coverage and companion measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_space_unit_key\", \"desc\": \"Space unit key columns identifying the organizational space-assignment unit across the space dimension and fact tables. SPACE_UNIT_KEY is the join key linking SPACE_DETAIL room rows to space unit identity (name/code) and, through SPACE_UNIT, to the owning facilities organization.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_assignable_area\", \"desc\": \"Assignable-area measure columns at different granularity levels and time semantics: building-level current and per-fiscal-period assignable area, floor-level assignable area, and the space-domain assignable square footage. All FCLT_*/FAC_* columns are in square meters; BUILDINGS.BLDG_ASSIGNABLE_SQUARE_FOOTAGE is in square feet. Choosing the right column determines whether the measure is a building total, a floor total, a historical value, or a space-assignment figure.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_facility_organization_key\", \"desc\": \"Facility organization key columns attributing space units and rooms to organizations in the hierarchical organization tree. Two naming conventions exist across table families (FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY in FCLT_*/SPACE_* tables vs ORGANIZATION_KEY in FAC_* tables) with the same value domain.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Phase 1 complete. Now Phase 2 — investigating the key entities in detail.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_95f2f899b6bd40c08d42bb94",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "semantic_get",
            "arguments": "{\"entity_ids\": \n[\"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"column_concept_total_units\", \"column_concept_department_name\", \"concept_department_dimension\", \"concept_academic_term_dimension\"]\n\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "call_7761f112d8344b7097d7429b",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "semantic_get",
            "arguments": "{\"entity_id\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\"}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_95f2f899b6bd40c08d42bb94",
      "name": "semantic_get",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"id\": \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\", \"name\": \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS administrative department table with administrative department code/name, phone area code and phone number, and clearing cost collector. Joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT via SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE for department contact information.\", \"columns\": {\"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}, \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Administrative department code; joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Administrative department name\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_PHONE_AREA_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Area code of the department phone number\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_PHONE_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Phone number of the administrative department\"}, \"CLEARING_COST_COLLECTOR\": {\"desc\": \"Clearing cost collector of the administrative department\"}, \"LAST_ACTIVITY_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Date of last activity on the record\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per administrative department\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"name\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS department dimension table: academic departments with code, name, full name, school attribution (code and name), budget code, degree-granting flag, and commencement-book names. Joins to subject offering tables via department codes.\", \"columns\": {\"DEPARTMENT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Department code; joins to offering tables' DEPARTMENT_CODE/OFFER_DEPT_CODE and SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department name, e.g. 'Mathematics', 'Chemistry'\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Full official name of the department\"}, \"SCHOOL_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"School code the department belongs to, e.g. 'E'\"}, \"SCHOOL_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"School name the department belongs to, e.g. 'Engineering'; used for school-level filtering\"}, \"DEPT_BUDGET_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Budget code of the department; used for budget-based ordering/ranking\"}, \"IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the department is degree granting\"}, \"DEPT_NAME_IN_COMMENCEMENT_BK\": {\"desc\": \"Department name as printed in the commencement book\"}, \"SCHOOL_NAME_IN_COMMENCEMENT_BK\": {\"desc\": \"School name as printed in the commencement book\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_NAME_HISTORY\": {\"desc\": \"Historical names of the department\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_LAST_ACTIVITY_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Date of last activity on the department record\"}, \"DLC_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Degree-granting list/committee key\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per academic department\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"name\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"desc\": \"Academic term dimension table describing each academic term's calendar and status attributes: term code/description, start/end dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, key registration and class dates, and term status classification (Previous/Current/Future, regular vs non-regular term). Used to filter and enrich subject offerings by term characteristics.\", \"columns\": {\"ACADEMIC_TERMS_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the academic term record; joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_TERMS_KEY\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code in YYYYTT format, e.g. '2025FA' (FA=Fall, SP=Spring, JA=January/IAP, SU=Summer)\"}, \"TERM_DESCRIPTION\": {\"desc\": \"Human-readable term description, e.g. 'Fall Term 2024-2025'\"}, \"TERM_SELECTOR\": {\"desc\": \"Term selector label used for picklists\"}, \"TERM_START_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Term start date; can match TIME_DAY.CALENDAR_DATE for calendar-based joins\"}, \"TERM_END_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Term end date\"}, \"ACADEMIC_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"Academic year the term belongs to, e.g. 2025\"}, \"ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Academic year description text\"}, \"IS_CURRENT_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag indicating whether the term is the current term\"}, \"IS_REGULAR_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag indicating a regular term (Fall/Spring) versus non-regular terms (Summer, January/IAP); only present in ACADEMIC_TERMS, not in ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\"}, \"TERM_STATUS_INDICATOR\": {\"desc\": \"Single-character term status indicator: 'P'=Previous, 'C'=Current, 'F'=Future, 'None'=Unspecified\"}, \"TERM_STATUS\": {\"desc\": \"Term status text: 'Previous', 'Current', 'Future', or 'Unspecified'\"}, \"FINANCIAL_AID_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"Financial aid year the term maps to\"}, \"DEGREE_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"Degree year the term maps to; used in degree-year statistics\"}, \"LAST_DAY_OF_FINAL_EXAM\": {\"desc\": \"Last day of final exams for the term\"}, \"PRE_REGISTRATION_START_DAY\": {\"desc\": \"First day of pre-registration for the term\"}, \"REGISTRATION_DAY\": {\"desc\": \"Registration day for the term\"}, \"FIRST_DAY_OF_CLASSES\": {\"desc\": \"First day of classes in the term\"}, \"LAST_DAY_OF_CLASSES\": {\"desc\": \"Last day of classes in the term\"}, \"ADD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Last day to add a subject in the term; only present in ACADEMIC_TERMS\"}, \"DROP_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Last day to drop a subject in the term; only present in ACADEMIC_TERMS\"}, \"GRADUATE_AWARD_START_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Start date of the graduate award period for the term\"}, \"GRADUATE_AWARD_END_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"End date of the graduate award period for the term\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date of the record\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per academic term\"}, {\"columns\": [\"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\", \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\", \"DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Source process\", \"detail\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS is the catalog-declared unit value per offering; SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS and SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS are registrar subject-level values; CIS/DRUPAL catalog feeds carry their own copies\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Companion unit columns\", \"detail\": \"All these tables also expose LECTURE_UNITS, LAB_UNITS, and preparation units (PREPARATION_UNITS except SUBJECT_SUMMARY which uses PREP_UNITS); DESIGN_UNITS exists in COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, CIS and DRUPAL catalogs but not in SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Variability flag\", \"detail\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.IS_VARIABLE_UNITS marks subjects whose units vary; analyses of fixed-unit statistics typically filter IS_VARIABLE_UNITS='N'\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Unit statistics (avg/stddev/variance/geometric mean) over catalog offerings, optionally split by lecture/lab/design or filtered by variable-units flag\": \"Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS with its companion unit columns.\", \"Unit statistics tied to actual enrollment records or subject groups per term\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS.\", \"Unit statistics at subject-offering rollup level with offering department/school\": \"Use SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS.\", \"Fixed-unit analyses excluding variable-unit subjects\": \"Filter COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.IS_VARIABLE_UNITS = 'N'.\"}, \"desc\": \"Total credit unit columns replicated across catalog and registrar subject tables. They represent the same business quantity (total credit units of a subject) but come from different processes and pair with different companion unit columns.\", \"id\": \"column_concept_total_units\", \"name\": \"Total Credit Units\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"name\": \"Department Name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\", \"columns\": [\"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT\", \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Naming convention\", \"detail\": \"DEPARTMENT_NAME is used by catalog/summary tables (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY), department/course lookup tables, and the student directory (MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY); OFFER_DEPT_NAME is used by offering/program tables (SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED) and denotes the department that actually offers the subject; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR uses the plain column name DEPARTMENT for the course's academic department; SE_PERSON uses ORGANIZATION for the person's organizational unit\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Value format\", \"detail\": \"Catalog, summary, offering, student-directory, and lookup tables store plain department names (e.g. 'Mathematics', 'Chemistry', 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'); LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT stores a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics', '06 - Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'), with some unprefixed values (e.g. 'Architecture'), so it is not directly comparable to plain-name columns without stripping the prefix\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Academic vs HR/organization value domain\", \"detail\": \"Catalog, summary, offering, library, student-directory, and lookup tables share the academic department domain; EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME is the HR organizational unit name and has a different domain (e.g. 'Lincoln Laboratory', 'Department of Physics'), where some values coincide with academic names but many do not, and some carry a 'Department of ...' prefix; SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION holds organizational unit names that may use different naming variants than the academic domain for the same unit (e.g. 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science' vs the academic 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'), so equality filters across the two conventions must use each table's own variant\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Companion code column\", \"detail\": \"Catalog/summary tables carry DEPARTMENT_CODE joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; offering/program tables carry OFFER_DEPT_CODE joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE or STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY carries DEPARTMENT (the academic department code) joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, which is the reliable join key instead of the name; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR has no department code column, only the prefixed name text; EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY carries DEPARTMENT_NUMBER (HR department number) and SE_PERSON carries no department code, neither joining to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Filtering subjects by department in catalog or summary analysis\": \"Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME or SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME.\", \"Filtering by department in section-level, textbook-program, or library analysis\": \"Use the OFFER_DEPT_NAME column of SUBJECT_OFFERED / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\", \"Joining fact tables to department dimension attributes (school, full name, degree-granting)\": \"Prefer code joins: DEPARTMENT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_CODE = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; name equality joins are used when codes are unavailable.\", \"Matching departments across a DEPARTMENT_NAME table and an OFFER_DEPT_NAME table\": \"The values are directly comparable (same academic name domain), e.g. joining SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME.\", \"Filtering employees by their HR organizational unit (e.g. names containing 'Department', or HR units like 'Political Science')\": \"Use EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME; do not join it to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, and pair it with DEPARTMENT_NUMBER for HR grouping.\", \"Filtering by department in section-level, textbook-program, or library subject analysis\": \"Use the OFFER_DEPT_NAME column of SUBJECT_OFFERED / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\", \"Filtering library reserve course instructors by academic department or library unit\": \"Use LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT with the prefixed value format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); do not compare it directly to plain department-name columns.\", \"Filtering students by their academic department\": \"Use MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT (code) joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE for reliable matching, or MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME for direct name filters; the name shares the academic domain with SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME.\", \"Filtering a person master (SE_PERSON) record by organizational unit such as an academic department\": \"Use SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION with its own naming variant (e.g. 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science'); do not equate it directly to MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME or SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, which use the academic variant (e.g. 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci').\"}}, {\"id\": \"concept_department_dimension\", \"name\": \"Department and School Dimension\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables describing academic departments and their school attribution: the SIS department dimension, the student-facing department lookup, and the SIS administrative department (contact information). They answer questions about department names, full names, school code/name, degree-granting status, budget codes, and department phone numbers, but differ in attribute coverage.\", \"tables\": [\"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Attribute coverage\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\": \"Richest: DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, SCHOOL_CODE/SCHOOL_NAME, DEPT_BUDGET_CODE, IS_DEGREE_GRANTING, commencement-book names, DLC key\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\": \"Minimal: code, name, full name, school code/name only\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\": \"Administrative contact: department phone area code/number, clearing cost collector\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Degree-granting and school filtering\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\": \"Supports IS_DEGREE_GRANTING and SCHOOL_NAME filters directly\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\": \"Only school code/name attribution, no degree-granting flag\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\": \"No school or degree-granting attributes\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Typical join path\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\": \"DEPARTMENT_CODE = offering tables' DEPARTMENT_CODE/OFFER_DEPT_CODE; also joins SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT and SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT.SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\": \"DEPARTMENT_CODE = TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE and other offering department codes\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\": \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Budget/finance attributes\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\": \"DEPT_BUDGET_CODE available for budget-based ranking\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\": \"None\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\": \"CLEARING_COST_COLLECTOR\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions filtering departments by school (e.g. 'School of Engineering') or degree-granting status\": \"Use SIS_DEPARTMENT; it carries SCHOOL_NAME and IS_DEGREE_GRANTING.\", \"Questions needing only department full name and school name for offering departments (e.g. TIP subject offerings)\": \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT suffices and is the lighter lookup; SIS_DEPARTMENT also works.\", \"Questions needing department phone numbers or administrative contact details\": \"Join SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT via SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE = SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE.\", \"Questions ranking or grouping departments by budget code\": \"Use SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPT_BUDGET_CODE.\"}}, {\"id\": \"concept_academic_term_dimension\", \"name\": \"Academic Term Dimension\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing academic terms and their calendar/status attributes. They jointly answer questions about when terms run, which academic/financial-aid/degree year a term belongs to, and whether a term is current, previous, future, or regular. Coverage differs: the full historical term list, the status-tracked term subset, and the three-row relative term parameter reference.\", \"tables\": [\"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\", \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Row coverage\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\": \"Terms with full status tracking (subset of all terms)\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\": \"All terms known to the warehouse (superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS)\", \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\": \"Exactly 3 rows: current, previous, and upcoming term\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Unique columns\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\": \"IS_REGULAR_TERM, TERM_STATUS ('Previous'/'Current'/'Future'/'Unspecified'), ADD_DATE, DROP_DATE\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\": \"No IS_REGULAR_TERM/TERM_STATUS/ADD_DATE/DROP_DATE; shares TERM_STATUS_INDICATOR, FINANCIAL_AID_YEAR, DEGREE_YEAR\", \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\": \"TERM_PARAMETER name (SIS_CURRENT_TERM/SIS_PREVIOUS_TERM/SIS_UPCOMING_TERM), TERM_INDICATOR ('C'/'P'/'F'), TERM_LAST_DAY_BEFORE_NEXT_TERM\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Typical role in queries\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\": \"Filtering by regular-term flag or term status; term start/end dates and registration milestones\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\": \"Source of academic year, academic year description, financial aid year, degree year for windowed/running-sum statistics\", \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\": \"Resolving relative term references ('current term', 'previous term', term indicator 'C'/'P') to concrete term codes\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Join keys\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\": \"TERM_CODE, ACADEMIC_TERMS_KEY\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\": \"TERM_CODE, ACADEMIC_TERMS_KEY\", \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\": \"TERM_CODE\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions needing IS_REGULAR_TERM or TERM_STATUS ('Previous'/'Current'/'Future') filtering\": \"Use ACADEMIC_TERMS; these columns exist only there.\", \"Questions needing academic year, financial aid year, or degree year attributes over the widest term coverage, or joining fact tables whose terms may not be status-tracked\": \"Use ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, optionally joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS on TERM_CODE when regular-term/status flags are also needed.\", \"Questions referring to 'the current term', 'the previous term', 'the upcoming term', or term indicator 'C'/'P'/'F'\": \"Use ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER to resolve the relative reference to a TERM_CODE, then join ACADEMIC_TERMS for full attributes.\", \"Questions needing registration milestones (add date, drop date, first day of classes, last day of final exam)\": \"Use ACADEMIC_TERMS (ADD_DATE/DROP_DATE only exist there; other milestone dates exist in both ACADEMIC_TERMS and ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL).\"}}], \"not_found\": []}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_7761f112d8344b7097d7429b",
      "name": "semantic_get",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entity\": {\"id\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Course catalog subject offering table recording catalog-level attributes of each subject offered per academic year and term: subject identity (SUBJECT_ID = SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_NUMBER), department, unit structure (lecture/lab/preparation/design/total units), grading type and rules, HGN level (Undergraduate/Graduate/High Graduate), requirement attributes (GIR, HASS, communication, writing), term offering flags (this year, fall, IAP, spring, summer), instructors, section flags, responsible faculty, and meeting time/place. Links to terms via both TERM_CODE (the offering term) and EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE (the term from which catalog attributes take effect).\", \"columns\": {\"ACADEMIC_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"Academic year of the catalog offering, e.g. 2022\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code of the offering record in YYYYTT format; joins to term tables\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier formed as SUBJECT_CODE + '.' + SUBJECT_NUMBER, e.g. '18.01'; joins to TIP_DETAIL, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY subject IDs\"}, \"SUBJECT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Subject/course code prefix, e.g. '18' for Mathematics; joins to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE and SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE\"}, \"SUBJECT_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Subject number within the subject code, e.g. '01'\"}, \"SOURCE_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Source system subject identifier\"}, \"PRINT_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier as printed in the bulletin\"}, \"IS_PRINTED_IN_BULLETIN\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject is printed in the bulletin\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Offering department code; joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Offering department name, e.g. 'Mathematics', 'Chemistry'\"}, \"EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code from which the catalog attributes of this subject take effect; frequently joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE for term-status filtering\"}, \"SUBJECT_SHORT_TITLE\": {\"desc\": \"Short title of the subject\"}, \"SUBJECT_TITLE\": {\"desc\": \"Full title of the subject\"}, \"IS_VARIABLE_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject has variable units\"}, \"LECTURE_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Number of lecture credit units\"}, \"LAB_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Number of lab credit units\"}, \"PREPARATION_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Number of preparation (outside-class) credit units\"}, \"TOTAL_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Total credit units of the subject (lecture+lab+preparation unless variable)\"}, \"DESIGN_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Number of design credit units\"}, \"GRADE_TYPE\": {\"desc\": \"Grade type code, e.g. 'L' = letter graded\"}, \"GRADE_TYPE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Grade type description\"}, \"GRADE_RULE\": {\"desc\": \"Grade rule code\"}, \"GRADE_RULE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Grade rule description, e.g. 'Not repeatable for credit'\"}, \"HGN_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"HGN (Higgins) level code\"}, \"HGN_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"HGN level description: 'Undergraduate', 'Graduate', or 'High Graduate'\"}, \"HGN_EXCEPT\": {\"desc\": \"HGN exception indicator\"}, \"GIR_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"General Institute Requirement attribute code\"}, \"GIR_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"General Institute Requirement attribute description\"}, \"COMM_REQ_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"Communication requirement attribute code\"}, \"COMM_REQ_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Communication requirement attribute description\"}, \"TUITION_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"Tuition attribute code\"}, \"TUITION_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Tuition attribute description\"}, \"WRITE_REQ_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"Writing requirement attribute code\"}, \"WRITE_REQ_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Writing requirement attribute description\"}, \"SUPERVISOR_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"Supervisor attribute code\"}, \"SUPERVISOR_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Supervisor attribute description\"}, \"PREREQUISITES\": {\"desc\": \"Prerequisite text for the subject\"}, \"SUBJECT_DESCRIPTION\": {\"desc\": \"Full catalog description text of the subject\"}, \"JOINT_SUBJECTS\": {\"desc\": \"List of joint subjects\"}, \"SCHOOL_WIDE_ELECTIVES\": {\"desc\": \"School-wide elective attribute\"}, \"MEETS_WITH_SUBJECTS\": {\"desc\": \"Subjects this one meets with\"}, \"EQUIVALENT_SUBJECTS\": {\"desc\": \"Equivalent subjects\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject is offered in the current academic year\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject is offered in the fall term\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_IAP\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject is offered during IAP (January)\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_SPRING_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject is offered in the spring term\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_SUMMER_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject is offered in the summer term\"}, \"FALL_INSTRUCTORS\": {\"desc\": \"Fall term instructor names\"}, \"SPRING_INSTRUCTORS\": {\"desc\": \"Spring term instructor names\"}, \"STATUS_CHANGE\": {\"desc\": \"Catalog status change indicator\"}, \"LAST_ACTIVITY_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Date of last activity on the record\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Master subject identifier when the subject is part of a cluster\"}, \"HASS_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute code\"}, \"HASS_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"HASS attribute description\"}, \"TERM_DURATION\": {\"desc\": \"Duration of the subject within the term\"}, \"GLOBAL_REGIONS\": {\"desc\": \"Global regions associated with the subject\"}, \"GLOBAL_COUNTRIES\": {\"desc\": \"Global countries associated with the subject\"}, \"ON_LINE_PAGE_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Online catalog page number\"}, \"SECTION_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Section identifier of the subject offering\"}, \"IS_MASTER_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for master section\"}, \"IS_LECTURE_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for lecture section\"}, \"IS_LAB_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for lab section\"}, \"IS_RECITATION_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for recitation section\"}, \"IS_DESIGN_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for design section\"}, \"RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the faculty member responsible for the subject\"}, \"RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"MIT ID of the responsible faculty member\"}, \"MEET_TIME\": {\"desc\": \"Meeting time text of the subject\"}, \"MEET_PLACE\": {\"desc\": \"Meeting place; stores the FCLT room key and joins to FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ROOM_KEY for facility/space analysis\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per subject offering per term/academic year\"}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Now let me look at precedent metrics that use regular terms and CV/STDDEV on TOTAL_UNITS, to see their SQL patterns.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
