      "content": "The database remains inaccessible (persistent `Access denied` authentication error on every attempt, including `SELECT 1`), so verification against live data is impossible; I'll ground the final SQL entirely in the semantic-network evidence and precedent metric SQL. Here is the full report.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (Phase 1 survivors relevant to the task):**\n\n- **SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT** — \"SIS administrative department table with administrative department code/name, phone area code and phone number, and clearing cost collector.\" Granularity: one row per administrative department. Key columns: `SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE` (\"joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"), `SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_NAME` (\"Administrative department name\").\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — academic department dimension: `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME` (\"e.g. 'Mathematics', 'Chemistry'\"), `DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME`, `SCHOOL_CODE/SCHOOL_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`, budget code, commencement-book names. One row per academic department.\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — catalog-level subject offerings per academic year and term: `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `TERM_CODE` (offering term), `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE` (\"term code from which the catalog attributes of this subject take effect; **frequently joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE for term-status filtering**\"), `DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `TOTAL_UNITS` (\"Total credit units of the subject\"), `SUBJECT_ID`, `IS_VARIABLE_UNITS`. Granularity: one row per subject offering per term/academic year.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS** — term dimension with `TERM_CODE`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `IS_REGULAR_TERM` (\"'Y'/'N' flag indicating a regular term (Fall/Spring) versus non-regular terms (Summer, January/IAP); **only present in ACADEMIC_TERMS, not in ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL**\"), `IS_CURRENT_TERM`, `TERM_STATUS_INDICATOR`. One row per term.\n\n**Related tables found but not needed (kept for completeness):** ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (superset of terms but **lacks IS_REGULAR_TERM** — cannot satisfy the \"regular academic terms\" filter), STUDENT_DEPARTMENT (lighter department lookup, no admin-department link), SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED / TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED / CIS_COURSE_CATALOG / DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG (alternative subject-offering facts; the task's column mapping anchors \"total units\" and \"academic year 2024\" to COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED).\n\n**Metrics (precedents):** dw_4640 (CV = `STDDEV(x)/NULLIF(AVG(x),0)` per department), dw_1049 (STDDEV of TOTAL_UNITS with `IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y'`), dw_3417 & dw_359 (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS via **EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE** with `IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y'`), dw_4387 (same via TERM_CODE), dw_1393 (SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT joined via `SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE = SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE`), dw_1471 (`ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2024` filter on the catalog table joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT_CODE), dw_2597, dw_41, dw_3237, dw_4231, dw_1335, dw_3311, dw_3644, dw_2958, dw_1023, dw_2151, dw_2272, dw_1471, dw_2224, dw_1833, dw_1465, dw_4025, dw_3235, dw_1288, dw_2151.\n\n**Concepts:** concept_department_dimension, concept_academic_term_dimension, concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_course_catalog_sources.\n\n**Column concepts:** column_concept_total_units, column_concept_department_name, column_concept_term_code, column_concept_year_columns.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\n- `SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT` graph neighbors (retrieved): joins ← SIS_DEPARTMENT (via `SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE`), joins ← MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, concept ← concept_department_dimension.\n- `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED` joins (retrieved): → ACADEMIC_TERMS, → ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, → SIS_DEPARTMENT, → SIS_SUBJECT_CODE, → SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, → FCLT_ROOMS, → EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY, → CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE, → SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE; ← SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL, TIP_DETAIL.\n- `column_concept_total_units` members: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS, SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS, DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG.TOTAL_UNITS. Decision guide: \"Unit statistics (avg/stddev/variance...) over catalog offerings → Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS.\"\n- `concept_academic_term_dimension` decision guide: \"Questions needing IS_REGULAR_TERM or TERM_STATUS filtering → Use ACADEMIC_TERMS; these columns exist only there.\"\n- Hint-provided join keys: SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT.SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE ↔ SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_CODE ↔ SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE ↔ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE **and** ↔ EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (key candidates):**\n\n| Dimension | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED | SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY | ACADEMIC_TERMS | ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL | SIS_DEPARTMENT | SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | one row per subject offering per term/academic year (retrieved) | subject/section per term (retrieved desc) | one row per term | one row per term (superset) | one row per department | one row per admin department |\n| TOTAL_UNITS | yes, catalog-declared (column_concept_total_units) | yes, registrar values | — | — | — | — |\n| ACADEMIC_YEAR column | yes (retrieved columns) | via term join | yes | yes | — | — |\n| IS_REGULAR_TERM | — | — | **yes, only here** (retrieved) | **no** (retrieved) | — | — |\n| Admin dept name | — | — | — | — | — | SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_NAME (retrieved) |\n| Fan-out risk | joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT/ACADEMIC_TERMS are 1:1 on unique keys (dimension granularities above) | n/a | n/a | n/a | n/a | n/a |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n\n| Requirement | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED | SUBJECT_* tables | ACADEMIC_TERMS | ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| measure: total units | SUPPORTED (TOTAL_UNITS; hint mapping) | SUPPORTED but not hint-mapped | — | — |\n| filter: academic year 2024 | SUPPORTED (ACADEMIC_YEAR; hint mapping \"academic year 2024: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR\") | NOT-SUPPORTED directly | SUPPORTED (ACADEMIC_YEAR) | SUPPORTED |\n| filter: regular terms | needs term join | needs term join | SUPPORTED (IS_REGULAR_TERM) | VIOLATES (column absent — retrieved comparison) |\n| key: department name / ≠ Mathematics | SUPPORTED (DEPARTMENT_NAME; hint mapping \"'Mathematics' (Course 18): COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\") | SUPPORTED | — | — |\n| admin dept name | NOT-SUPPORTED | NOT-SUPPORTED | — | — (requires SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT) |\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"administrative department name\" → `SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT.SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_NAME` (only column with this semantics; hint mapping confirms).\n- \"'Mechanical Engineering' (Course 2)\" → filter `SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mechanical Engineering'` (hint mapping).\n- \"academic year 2024\" → `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2024` (hint mapping; precedent dw_1471 uses exactly `t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2024`).\n- \"'Mathematics' (Course 18)\" exclusion → `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Mathematics'` (hint mapping).\n- \"regular academic terms\" → `ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'` (hint mapping; concept decision guide says this column exists only in ACADEMIC_TERMS).\n- \"number of subjects\" → hint maps it to `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS`, i.e. `COUNT(TOTAL_UNITS)` over the catalog rows in regular terms.\n- Ambiguity: TERM_CODE vs EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE for the regular-term join — both are listed in the hints. Discriminating evidence: the retrieved column definition of `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE` says it is \"frequently joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE for term-status filtering\", and precedents dw_3417/dw_359 (IS_REGULAR_TERM filters on this catalog table) use EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE, while dw_4387 uses TERM_CODE (2 vs 1 precedent count; column-definition evidence favors EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE for status filtering).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:**\n- CV precedents (`STDDEV/AVG`): 1 — dw_4640 (`STDDEV(x)/NULLIF(AVG(x),0)` per department).\n- STDDEV-of-TOTAL_UNITS + IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y' precedents: 3 — dw_1049 (TERM_CODE join, SUBJECT_SUMMARY), dw_3417 (EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE join, catalog table), dw_359 (EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE join, catalog table); plus dw_4387 (TERM_CODE join, catalog table, AVG).\n- SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT ↔ SIS_DEPARTMENT join precedent: dw_1393 (`d.DEPARTMENT_CODE = ad.SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE`).\n- ACADEMIC_YEAR=2024 on catalog joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT_CODE: dw_1471.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: consumed by dozens of unit-statistics metrics (dw_2151, dw_1471, dw_3417, dw_359, dw_41, dw_2597, dw_4387…); the column_concept_total_units decision guide directs catalog unit statistics here.\n- **SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT**: used for admin department name/phone/clearing-cost questions (dw_1393, dw_2224, dw_1427, dw_1983, dw_2240); always joined through SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE.\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT**: the canonical department dimension for code↔name↔school↔degree-granting resolution; joins to all offering tables via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS**: the only source of IS_REGULAR_TERM/TERM_STATUS; used to filter offerings to Fall/Spring regular terms (dw_1049, dw_3417, dw_359, dw_4387).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓, semantic_graph(query_neighbors) ✓\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓, semantic_graph(joins) ✓\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS / ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓\n- concept_department_dimension, concept_academic_term_dimension — semantic_get ✓\n- column_concept_total_units, column_concept_department_name — semantic_get ✓\n- Precedent metrics dw_1049, dw_359, dw_4640, dw_1393, dw_3417, dw_41, dw_2597, dw_1471, dw_4231, dw_3237, dw_4387 — semantic_get ✓\n- mysql_query — attempted 6 times; **all failed with `Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'` (infrastructure error, not a SQL error)**; live verification impossible, noted explicitly.\n- Other Phase-1 entities (SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED(_SUMMARY), TIP/LIBRARY tables, CIS/DRUPAL catalogs, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, unrelated facilities/HR/space entities) — screened via retrieved descriptions; facilities/space/HR entities discarded as completely unrelated to departments/subjects/units/terms.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:** SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT (`SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_NAME` filter+output), SIS_DEPARTMENT (bridge via `DEPARTMENT_CODE`), COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (`ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `TOTAL_UNITS`, `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE`), ACADEMIC_TERMS (`TERM_CODE`, `IS_REGULAR_TERM`).\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** Two CTEs cross-joined: (1) admin-department CTE — join SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT → SIS_DEPARTMENT → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED on department codes, filter name='Mechanical Engineering' and ACADEMIC_YEAR=2024, compute `STDDEV(TOTAL_UNITS)/NULLIF(AVG(TOTAL_UNITS),0)`; (2) department CTE — join COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED → ACADEMIC_TERMS on `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE = TERM_CODE` with `IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y'`, exclude `DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics'`, group by department (via SIS_DEPARTMENT), compute CV and `COUNT(TOTAL_UNITS)`. All joins are to unique-key dimensions (no fan-out). No rounding applied.\n\n**6c. Reasons:** *Data* — catalog table is one row per subject offering per term/year and physically carries ACADEMIC_YEAR, TOTAL_UNITS, DEPARTMENT_NAME/CODE (retrieved columns); dimension joins are 1:1 so no fan-out. *Semantic-network* — hint mappings anchor every phrase to these exact columns; column_concept_total_units decision guide directs unit statistics to COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS; concept_academic_term_dimension states IS_REGULAR_TERM exists only in ACADEMIC_TERMS; EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE's definition says it is \"frequently joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE for term-status filtering\". *Business* — dw_4640 establishes the CV formula shape (`STDDEV/NULLIF(AVG,0)`); dw_3417/dw_359 establish the EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE + IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y' pattern on this catalog table; dw_1393 establishes the admin-department join path; dw_1471 establishes `ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2024` on the catalog table.\n\n**6d. Alternative/tie-breaker:** dw_4387 uses `TERM_CODE` instead of `EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE` for regular-term filtering; the column-definition evidence and 2-vs-1 precedent count favor EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE. Live join-match rates would break the tie definitively, but the database is inaccessible (authentication failure on every attempt).\n\n**Final SQL** (SELECT list exactly matches the 5 requested outputs, in order):\n\n",
